# TEST ONLY: force the Bandicoot Pursuit chase to start, so the rig can watch Evil Crash steer.
# He normally waits for user message 269 (sent by the summoner once it has a focus object) and then branches on
# counter 26. Neither happens from a level warp. Both edits are size-neutral, so the save states stay valid.
#
# RUN 2026-09-21, and it does not produce a chase - but the edit is not what is wrong. Evil Crash is placed
# at (85.4, 1.6, -91.2) in altdoc, (-164.71, 0, -60.8) in altdoc_b and (-127.59, 0.33, 102.4) in altdoc_c,
# and all three files warp Crash to the same (91.15, 0.02, -154.81): they carry no start marker, so they
# share a default spawn. Walking out of it with goto covers about 18 units before the stick stops moving him,
# blocked by geometry rather than a fall. The spawn is a pocket that does not reach him in any of the three.
#
# An earlier note here said both actors read position (0,0,0) and so were placed nowhere near the player.
# That evidence was worthless - +0xD0 is the position on a character context and neither of them is one, the
# same reason findactor cannot see crates. The placements above are the real reason.
#
# Worth keeping anyway, because the edit itself is sound and will be wanted the moment a playthrough save
# exists. One caveat to remember when that happens: message 269 is not only a go signal - state 1's body runs
# RequestMessSourceAsFocus, which takes its focus from the sender, so skipping the message also skips the
# focus. The summoner's own script branches to COM_GENERIC_CREATURE_ERROR when GotFocusObject is false, which
# is the same failure by another route. Its focus search, script 5175 state 6 body 0, can be appended to
# state 1 with `appendcmds 5177 1 0 5175 6 0` if that turns out to be needed.
#
file Levels\AltEarth\Hub\altdoc.rm2
setcond 5177 1 0 5 0 0 3.0   # COM_ALTEARTH_DOCAMOK_EVILCRASH_DEFAULT state 1: GotUserMessageEquals(269) -> TimeInUnit 3s
setcond 5177 2 0 2 0         # state 2: CounterValueEqualsThreshold(26)==1 -> Else, so he always enters PHASE1
